>> title: Tuna Noodle Casserole
>> category: Noodles
>> tags: tuna, egg noodles, blue plate, casserole, oven
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: tuna casserole, tuna bake, tuna noodle bake, tuna mornay
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr

>> step: boil 6 min, two short of the box
Boil @wide egg noodles{8%oz}(225 g) in @water{4%qt}(3.8 L) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}(18 g) ~boil{6%min}, two minutes short of the box, because they finish in the oven.

>> step: sweat 5 min, then cook the flour in
Sweat @yellow onion{1%medium}(diced) and @celery{2%ribs}(diced) in @unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(57 g) in a #saucepan{} ~fry{5%min}, then cook @all-purpose flour{1/4%cup}(30 g) into them for a minute without letting it colour.

>> step: whisk in, simmer 5 min to a coating sauce
Whisk @whole milk{2%cup}(480 mL) and @chicken stock{1%cup}(240 mL) into @&(~1)onion roux{} a ladle at a time and ~simmer{5%min}, until it coats the back of a spoon.

>> step: melt the cheese in off the heat
Melt @sharp cheddar{4%oz}(115 g; grated), @Dijon mustard{2%tsp}(10 mL), @black pepper{1/2%tsp} and @lemon juice{2%tsp}(10 mL) into @&(~1)white sauce{} off the heat.

>> step: fold the lot together
Fold @&(~4)drained noodles{}, @oil-packed tuna{10%oz}(280 g; drained, in large flakes) and @frozen peas{1%cup}(140 g) into @&(~1)cheese sauce{} with a spatula, in big strokes — the tuna should stay in pieces you can see.

>> step: scatter the crumbs, bake 375°F (190°C) 25 min
Scatter @panko{1%cup}(50 g) tossed with @melted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) over @&(~1)casserole{} in a buttered dish and ~bake{25%min} at 375°F (190°C), until the top is brown and the edges bubble.
